## Data we collect

EuroZig.eu is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub stores the IP addresses of
visitors to this website for security reasons. The legal basis for this is a
legitimate interest on the part of Microsoft/GitHub. For further information,
please see [GitHub's privacy statement](https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement).

If you sign up to the mailing list, your e-mail address and optionally your
name are stored. This is necessary to send you the e-mails. The legal basis
for this is your consent.

If you would like your data to be deleted, please contact
[privacy@eurozig.eu](mailto:privacy@eurozig.eu).

## Responsible party

EuroZig e.V. (in founding), Leonhardstraße 20A, 90443 Nürnberg, Germany —
see the [imprint]($link.page('imprint')) for contact details.

## Your rights under the GDPR

Under the provisions of the GDPR, you are in principle entitled to the
following rights:

- Right to rectification (Article 16 GDPR)
- Right to erasure ("right to be forgotten") (Article 17 GDPR)
- Right to restriction of processing (Article 18 GDPR)
- Right to notification — notification obligation regarding rectification or
  erasure of personal data or restriction of processing (Article 19 GDPR)
- Right to data portability (Article 20 GDPR)
- Right to object (Article 21 GDPR)
- Right not to be subject to a decision based solely on automated
  processing — including profiling (Article 22 GDPR)
- If you believe that the processing of your data violates data protection
  law or that your data protection rights have otherwise been infringed, you
  can lodge a complaint with the Federal Commissioner for Data Protection
  and Freedom of Information (BfDI).
